AB  - The multimodal generative AI is revolutionizing patient guidance by moving away from static symptom checkers towards intelligent, context-aware healthcare ecosystems. The paper proposes a high-performance Generative AI-Driven Health Expert Twin that is intended for real-time clinical assistance. The proposed system is distinguished from existing text-based chatbots by its combination of large language models (LLMs) and retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) that is grounded on a massive 6-volume medical knowledge base: The Gale Encyclopedia of Medicine. The proposed system utilizes GROQ’s high-speed LLM inference models within a local environment to attain high-speed response time requirements for seamless voice, image, and text interactions. The proposed system is distinguished by its two-storage approach to medical knowledge retrieval using FAISS and patient memory preservation using SQLite. The proposed system is further distinguished by its Clinical Decision Support System (CDSS), which checks for drug interactions, generates emergency pop-up alerts for "Red Flag" symptoms, and generates telemedicine suggestions. The proposed system has been experimentally proven to attain significant improvements in diagnostic grounding and safety layer reliability, thereby offering a robust roadmap for scalability and privacy-aware digital health twins.
