AB  - The development of generative AI has the potential to transform healthcare by enabling intelligent handling of even complex clinical data. This article presents a novel method for helping medical professionals make difficult diagnostic decisions by combining Large Language Models (LLMs) and Vision-Language Models (VLMs) into a unified framework. The system implants two primary modules, a Magnetic Resonance Imaging Report Summarization Agent to summarize the mass reports and store valuable information in it and a Diagnosing Assistance Chatbot to promote interactive communication between patients and clinicians seeking to extract fine-grained details of the past cases given the contextual information. In addition to these text characteristics, VLMs can process X-rays and other diagnostic imaging texts end-to-end to make up a multi-modal pipeline to support real-world clinical situations. By combining knowledge of text and image, the model proposed is able to enhance diagnostic performance, and speed up decision making, and finally result in improved patient benefit
