AB  - Effective learning in modern education requires tools that not only store information but actively help learners retain knowledge and plan future careers. We present SmartEduNotes, a web-based, retrieval-augmented platform that enhances personal note-taking through dense semantic search, provenance-aware question answering, automated flashcard generation, and concept-graph-driven career guidance. The system integrates Sentence-BERT embeddings, FAISS vector search, and LLM-based generation to provide accurate, context-grounded answers from personal notes, while automatically converting content into cloze-style flashcards scheduled with our novel Adaptive SM-2 algorithm for optimized spaced repetition. Central concepts extracted via a concept graph inform personalized skill recommendations based on real-world job postings. Pilot evaluation on 150 lecture note documents demonstrates up to 87 % QA accuracy, 85% 7-day flashcard recall (compared to 62 % manually), and effective identification of career-relevant skills. The architecture supports modular expansion, multi-modal input (audio, text), on-device privacy, and adaptive learning strategies. This work contributes a reproducible framework for personalized learning, knowledge retention, and career-aligned skill development.
