AB  - In the last decade enormous number of online classes has started. Students are also engaging and learning from these platforms. In the result of this, the rise of video content on platforms like YouTube has made it a key resource for learning, but pull out expressive understandings from videos can be time-consuming and inefficient. Additionally, NPTEL course make a big impact on the education sector. It is the need of the current situation to have an application that capable of summarizing YouTube video transcripts and creating substantial MCQ, short questions answer based on the content, along with an unified chatbot intended to reaction of user queries and participate in conversations related to the summarized material and generated questions. This paper proposes the development of an application designed to enhance accessible educational resources by summarizing video transcripts or youtube video linkes and generating various questions type for assessment. We use the Large language model (LLM) and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) framework to generate the questions or summarization. This application transforms video consumption into an interactive and efficient learning experience, making it valuable for education, training, and beyond. Our work seeks to bridge the gap in student's self-assessment by offering various practice questions and a chatbot for addressing required queries. (Abstract)
