AB  - The proposed framework incorporates an enhanced Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG++) process to ensure accurate fact validation and employs sophisticated transformer-based models such as RoBERTa to analyze and evaluate textual data. A chatbot-powered interface allows users to submit claims or news articles for quick evaluation. The backend uses Generative AI to make contextually appropriate corrections and combines LLMs LangChain and OpenAI APIs to assess the authenticity of the content. By encouraging transparency in AI-assisted journalism and media analysis this framework strengthens the credibility of digital content and reduces the spread of false information. The proposed system achieved an F1-score of 0.94 and an overall accuracy of 95% outperforming existing approaches in all significant evaluation metrics. A confusion matrix is added to further validate the models robustness and dependability across fake and real news categories. Further research will focus on developing the framework to support multilingual and multimodal misinformation analysis that includes images and videos as well as incorporating continuous learning mechanisms to adapt to emerging trends in fake news.
