AB  - The real estate industry continues to rely on fragmented workflows for property discovery, lead handling, customer communication, appointment scheduling, and broker coordination. While digital listing portals have improved access to property information, most platforms still lack contextual intelligence and action-oriented automation. This paper presents SmartEstateGPT, an autonomous AI agent designed for real estate operations using Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), tool calling, and TurboQuant-based cost optimization. The proposed platform unifies semantic property search, conversational question answering, meeting scheduling, CRM synchronization, and contextual memory within a single modular architecture. A benchmark dataset containing 18,500 property records and 12,000 customer queries was constructed for experimentation. Comparative evaluation against rule-based chatbots, collaborative filtering recommenders, and non-RAG LLM baselines shows that the proposed approach achieves 94.1% accuracy, 91.3% precision, 89.8% recall, and 0.86 seconds average response latency. TurboQuant reduces KV-cache memory usage by 61% and lowers inference cost by 47%. Ablation studies confirm the contribution of each module to final performance. The results indicate that practical, scalable, and cost-efficient AI agents can significantly improve real estate operations.
