AB  - In Nepal, many citizens still struggle to access basic municipal services due to fragmented information systems, linguistic diversity, and limited digital literacy. We explore two approaches:fine-tuning a multilingual large language model and employing a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) framework that combines semantic retrieval with generative modeling. Our RAG-based system integrates semantic search, multilingual embeddings, and context-aware generation to deliver accurate and flexible responses. Experimental evaluation shows that the RAG-based system outperforms the fine-tuned model in semantic accuracy, robustness to paraphrasing, and factual consistency, achieving a BERTScore-F1 of 0.99 and BLEU of 0.93 on a held-out test set. Human evaluation on real user queries further confirms improved relevance and reduced hallucination in RAG outputs. The system demonstrates the potential of multilingual LLMs in providing inclusive and citizen-friendly public services in low-resource languages such as Nepali.
